# MAC-14 annotation (format: docs/asm/NOTES_FORMAT.md)
# Markers: no marker means verified from the code; [assumed] means assumption; [?] means unknown.

ptrtab D1C9 4      # dispatcher tasks
ptrtab DADF 16     # KW1281 commands

legend
|LEGEND MAC-14 (J88, Audi 100/200 typ 44, engine MC2)
|CPU HD63B03XP, ROM Fujitsu MBM27128 (16 KB, $C000-$FFFF), RAM $8000-$8290.
|External chip at address $0100/$0101 (register number / data): ADC, tooth counting,
|ignition, digital inputs. Its type has not been identified.
|Tick ≈ 10 ms [assumed, derived from the 5-baud receive code; tester tolerance ±10 %].
|Engine speed: 1 unit of $8018 ≈ 22…24 rpm [assumed], exact scale not confirmed.
|Port 2: P2DDR bit 1 = 1 makes all of P21-P27 outputs at once (HD6303X datasheet),
|so PORT2.5 (purpose unknown) and PORT2.6 (N75) work as outputs.
|Register $14 is RP5CR (RAM and port 5): bit 6 enables internal RAM $40-$FF,
|bit 7 is the RAM power-retention flag, bits 0/1 enable IRQ1/IRQ2. Tasks: 0 every tick,
|1 every 2 ticks, 2 every 4, 3 every 10 (table D1E1).
|
|Code         What it is                           Pin    Where in the program
|F            brake light switch                   32     chip, reg. $19 bit 3 [assumed]
|F60          idle switch                          20     chip, reg. $19 bit 5 [assumed]
|F76          coolant thermo switch > 119 °C       14     PORT5.7 [assumed]
|F81          full load switch                     26     chip, reg. $19 bit 4 [assumed]
|G4           TDC sender (flywheel pin)            13/12  chip, IRQ1 events [assumed]
|G28          engine speed (ring gear teeth)       11/29  chip, reg. $0C/$0D -> $8018
|G39          oxygen sensor                        30     ADC ch. 3 (10 bit) -> $801C
|G40          Hall sender in distributor           27/25  PORT6.1 (input)
|G42          intake air temperature               24     ADC ch. 7 -> $8020 [assumed]
|G61, G66     knock sensors                        15,2/16 ADC ch. 6 via amplifier [assumed]
|G62          coolant temperature                  10     ADC ch. 2 -> $801B [assumed]
|G71          manifold pressure (inside the unit)  —      ADC ch. 0 -> $8019 [assumed]
|J17          fuel pump relay                      21     PORT6.6, 1 = on [assumed]: off without sync,
|                                                          on in test 4433 (F930), off by protections (EF60)
|J128         boost gauge in the instrument cluster 17    not found [?]
|J142         idle control unit (signal input)     4      ADC ch. 5 -> $801E (N65) [assumed]
|K66 / L      VEZ lamp, blink code output          31     PORT6.4
|N7           mixture frequency valve              8      timer output OC1, 71.8 Hz; test 4441 = 50 %
|N17          cold start valve                     1      PORT6.5, 0 = open; test 4443
|N65          fuel cut-off (via J142)              4      see J142
|N70          ignition power stage                 22     chip $0100 [assumed]
|N75          boost control valve                  19     PORT2.6, PWM in the CMI interrupt; test 4442
|N80          carbon canister purge valve          3      chip, reg. $0B: 00/FF slow PWM; test 4343
|N115         tank shut-off valve                  23     chip, reg. $19 bit 2; test 4331
|—            L line (diagnostic request input)    5      PORT5.6
|—            K line (KW1281)                      28     SCI (P23 receive / P24 transmit)
|—            coding (connector T6m)               6, 34  PORT6.2 and PORT5.4, which goes where is [?]
|—            supply voltage                       35     ADC ch. 1 -> $801A [assumed]
|—            "program running" signal (watchdog) —     PORT6.7, toggled every tick; if it stops, an external circuit restarts the CPU [assumed]
|—            tachometer, J142                     7      PORT6.3 [assumed]
|—            unknown output                       ?      PORT2.5: 1 at engine speed ≥ 20 units after sync, 1 after reset [?]
|
|Blink codes ($C928), two fault memory bits per code:
|1111 ECU   2111 G28   2112 G4   2113 G40   2121 F60   2123 F81
|2141/2143 knock retard limit   2142 G61   2144 G66
|2214 overspeed   2221/2222 G71   2224 overboost
|2312 G62   2322 G42   2342 lambda control   4444 no faults
|(code meanings are taken from an older analysis and will be rechecked against the code)
|Actuator tests ($C958): 4433 J17, 4441 N7, 4442 N75, 4443 N17, 4343 N80, 4331 N115.
|Test step order: the bit in $80AF shifts right: $80 J17, $40 N7, $20 N75,
|$10 N17, $08 N80, $04 N115 (verified for N7, N75, N17, N80, N115).

# ---- tasks and vectors (root names)
label D220 TASK0
label DD18 TASK1
label E30A TASK2
label EA2C TASK3

# ======================================================================
# Common subroutines: axis search and interpolation (CA05-CA87)
# Typical call:  LDX #axis / LDAA value / LDAB #points / JSR AXIS_UP
#                PSHB / JSR FRAC_UP / TBA / PULB / LDX #table / ABX / TAB / JSR INTERP
# ======================================================================
label CA05 FRAC_UP
head CA05
|FRAC_UP: fraction between two points of an ascending axis.
|Input: A = value, X -> left axis point (result of AXIS_UP).
|Output: B = (A - axis[i]) * 256 / (axis[i+1] - axis[i]), i.e. 0...255.
CA05 B = 0 in case of an exact hit
CA06 A = value minus left point
CA08 exactly on the point? yes: fraction 0
CA0A B = interval width
CA0E divide
label CA10 FRAC_DN
head CA10
|FRAC_DN: the same for a descending axis (axis[i] > axis[i+1]).
CA10 B = 0 in case of an exact hit
CA11 A = left point minus value
CA14 exactly on the point? yes: fraction 0
CA16 B = interval width (positive)
label CA1B DIV8
head CA1B
|DIV8: fractional division: B = A * 256 / B. Condition: A < B.
|Ordinary long division, 8 steps. Quotient bits are accumulated
|inverted and flipped at the end (COMB).
CA1B push divisor
CA1C push dividend
CA1D room for the step counter
CA1F 8 steps
CA21 counter
CA23 A = dividend (remainder)
CA25 quotient: initial value FF (bits inverted)
CA27 save
CA29 B is the high part of the remainder
CA2A shift remainder left
CA2B carry into B
CA2C subtract divisor
CA2E account for borrow
CA30 not negative? yes: quotient bit 1 (written as 0 here because it is inverted)
CA32 went negative: add the divisor back
CA34 carry = 1 (quotient bit 0, written inverted)
CA36 quotient bit into the result
CA38 next step
CA3A steps left? yes: repeat
CA3C pop counter
CA3D B = inverted quotient
CA3E drop divisor
CA3F B = quotient (fraction 0...255)
CA40 return
label CA41 INTERP
head CA41
|INTERP: linear interpolation between two adjacent table values.
|Input: X -> table[i], B = fraction (0...255).
|Output: A = t[i] + (t[i+1] - t[i]) * fraction / 256, rounded.
CA41 t[i]
CA43 push
CA44 t[i+1]
CA46 push
CA47 X -> t[i+1] on the stack, followed by t[i]
CA48 A = t[i+1]; the sign will take its place
CA4A sign = 0 (rising)
CA4C A = t[i+1] - t[i]
CA4E table rising? yes: the difference is already positive
CA50 falling: absolute value of the difference
CA51 sign = FF (falling)
CA53 difference * fraction
CA54 rounding: top bit of the low byte
CA55 add it
CA57 B = sign
CA58 table rising?
CA59 yes: add
CA5B no: subtract
CA5C B = t[i]
CA5D A = t[i] + correction
CA5E return
label CA5F AXIS_UP
head CA5F
|AXIS_UP: find the interval on an ascending axis.
|Input: A = value, X -> axis, B = number of points.
|Output: X -> left point of the interval, B = its index, A = value.
|Below the first point: index 0 and A = first point (fraction will be 0).
|Above the last: last point and A = its value.
CA5F save value
CA60 save number of points
CA61 value below this point?
CA63 yes: interval found
CA65 next point
CA66 points left?
CA67 no: past the end of the axis
CA69 to the next one
label CA6B AXIS_DN
head CA6B
|AXIS_DN: the same for a descending axis (for example, temperature from the ADC:
|the colder, the larger the number).
CA6B save value
CA6C save number of points
CA6D value above this point?
CA6F yes: interval found
CA71 next point
CA72 points left?
CA73 yes: continue
CA75 past the end: B = number of points
CA76 A = value
CA77 index of the last point
CA78 X -> last point
CA79 A = point value (fraction will be 0)
CA7B return
CA7C A = number of points
CA7D A = index of the point found
CA7E into B
CA7F is this the first point (value before the start of the axis)?
CA81 no: left point = previous one
CA82 X -> left point
CA83 A = value
CA84 return
CA85 pop value; A = first point
CA86 to the common exit

# ======================================================================
# Throttle switches and the flag "G71 faulty under load" (D1E5-D21F)
# ======================================================================
label D1E5 IS_IDLE
head D1E5
|IS_IDLE: is the throttle closed (idle switch F60)?
|Output: C = 1 means closed. If engine speed is not below the first point of axis C210
|(40 units ≈ 890 rpm) and the idle switch is flagged as faulty ($8093.3),
|the answer is always "not closed".
D1E5 engine speed
D1E8 below 40 units (≈890 rpm)?
D1EB yes: trust the switch
D1ED idle switch fault bit
D1EF idle switch faulty?
D1F2 yes: treat the throttle as open
D1F4 read digital inputs (chip reg. $19)
D1F6 bit 5 is the idle switch F60
D1F8 open? yes: throttle open
D1FA closed: C = 1
D1FC C = 0: throttle open
label D1FE MAP_BAD_LOAD
head D1FE
|MAP_BAD_LOAD: is G71 faulty while the engine is under load?
|Output: C = 1 if there is a pressure fault ($8091 & $72), engine speed is not below
|40 units and the throttle is not closed. Then instead of the measured pressure
|the substitute value $C79E is used.
D1FE pressure fault bits
D200 any pressure faults?
D203 no: C = 0
D205 engine speed
D208 below 40 units (≈890 rpm)?
D20B yes: C = 0
D20D throttle closed?
D20F yes: C = 0
D211 C = 1: use the substitute pressure
D213 C = 0
label D215 RD_INPUTS
head D215
|RD_INPUTS: read chip register $19, the digital inputs.
|Bit 5 is F60 (idle), bit 4 is F81 (full throttle), bit 3 is the brake light switch,
|bit 2 reads back the N115 output. 1 = contact closed [assumed from the logic].
D215 register number $19
label D217 CHIP_RD
head D217
|CHIP_RD: read chip register $0100: A = number, on exit A = data.
|Interrupts are disabled so that an IRQ cannot change the register number between the write and the read.
D217 disable interrupts
D218 register number
D21B data
D21E enable interrupts

