# ======================================================================
# Task 3 (every 10 ticks = 100 ms): G42 snapshot, N80, N115, G28 check
# ======================================================================
head EA2C
|TASK 3, start. Intake air temperature snapshot $8206.
|$8206 = G42 ($8020), but it is updated only when the engine has been idling for 2 s
|in a row (throttle closed, engine speed below 40 units).
|While driving the snapshot is frozen, so intake heating while driving has no effect [assumed].
|The snapshot is used to choose the N115 threshold (EAE1). The first one is taken immediately.
EA2C snapshot never taken yet?
EA2F yes: take it now
EA31 throttle closed?
EA34 no: idle counter to zero
EA36 engine speed
EA39 below 40 units (≈890 rpm)?
EA3C yes: count idle time
EA3E not idling: counter = 0
EA41 leave the snapshot alone
EA43 idle time
EA46 already 20 calls (2 s)?
EA48 yes: update the snapshot
EA4A + 1
EA4B save
EA4E leave the snapshot alone for now
EA50 intake air temperature G42
EA53 $8206 = snapshot
EA56 is there sync ($8095.5)?
EA58 check
EA5B yes: N80 and N115
EA5D no: skip them
head EA60
|N80: carbon canister purge. Duty cycle $8064 = 0…31 of 32 steps
|of a slow PWM (step 5.09 ms, period 163 ms, output in the OCF interrupt, F5FA).
|For the first 255 calls (25.5 s) after sync there is no purging (C795).
|After that an 8×8 map: rows by pressure (axis C7B0 = 116 103 90 77 71 64 58 51),
|columns by engine speed (axis C7B8 = 40 53 67 80 93 107 120 160).
|Map C7C0 is the normal one, C800 is used when $8066.1 is set [?]. At idle
|a constant value C7AE = 8 (or C845 = 4 when $8066.1 is set).
