# ======================================================================
# Task 3: check of pressure sensor G71 (EB2A-EC5F, patch F760-F7D3)
# ======================================================================
head EB2A
|G71 check. Fault flags in $8091:
|  bit 0: F60 closed (its own copy of the input);
|  bit 7: suspicion countdown running (counter $809C);
|  bit 6: pressure above 243 with the throttle closed for 10 calls (1 s): sensor "stuck high";
|  bit 5: pressure below 13 with the throttle open for 1 s: sensor "stuck low";
|  bit 4: during the first 10 s after start the pressure never moved 13 away from atmospheric;
|  bit 2: pressure has moved away from atmospheric (sensor is alive);
|  bit 3: check of the first 10 s finished;
|  bit 1: pressure does not move when it should (see EC18 and patch F760).
|Bits 6 and 5 give code 2222, bits 4 and 1 give code 2221 (code assembly, F001).
|Atmospheric pressure is $8004, taken when the ignition is switched on.
|In $8093 here: bit 7 means F60 has just closed; bit 6 means waiting for the pressure
|to drop after the throttle closes; bit 5 means the pressure has dropped.
EB2A G71 flags
EB2D clear bit 0 first
EB2F digital inputs
