head EFD9
|Assembling the fault memory. Each byte $8000-$8002 holds 8 codes, bit 7 first.
|The order matches the blink code table $C928. Bits are only added
|(the memory is "sticky"); only clearing removes them. If a byte has changed,
|the counter of starts without changes $802B is reset to zero.
|$8000: 7 is 1111 ECU ($8095 & $C0); 6 is 2111 G28 ($8094.6); 5 is 2112 G4 ($8094.4);
|       4 is 2113 Hall ($8094.2); 3 is 2113 ($8094.0); 2 is 2222 G71 high ($8091.6);
|       1 is 2222 G71 low ($8091.5); 0 is 2221 G71 not moving ($8091 & $12).
|$8001: 7 is 2142 G61 ($80B6.6); 6 is 2144 G66 ($80B6.4); 5 is 2141 ($8051.3);
|       4 is 2143 ($8051.2); 3 is 2123 F81 ($8093.1); 2 is 2121 F60 ($8093.3);
|       1 is 2121 ($8093.2, never set in this calibration); 0 is 2322 G42 ($8092.5).
|$8002: 7 is 2322 G42 ($8092.4); 6 is 2312 G62 ($8092.3); 5 is 2312 ($8092.2);
|       4 is 2342 lambda ($8060.1); 3 is 2214 engine speed ($809F.2);
|       2 is 2224 overboost ($809F.1); 1 is 4444 "no faults"; 0 is end of list.
