# ======================================================================
# Task 3: pin 5 (L line): entry into blink codes and actuator test,
# test outputs N75/N80/N115 (F146-F225)
# ======================================================================
head F146
|L line (pin 5, PORT5.6). Pin connected to ground means PORT5.6 = 0 [assumed].
|Holding it closed for 25 calls (2.5 s) starts the output ($80A9.7 = 1).
|While the engine has never turned ($8003.4 = 0) this is the actuator test
|(F24D), otherwise the fault codes are output. In the test, opening the contact sets a request,
|and the step changes on the next closing of ≥ 2.5 s: the step bit in $80AF shifts right
|($80 J17, $40 N7, $20 N75, $10 N17, $08 N80, $04 N115).
|The same start can come from the tester via the K line ($80F7.3).
