# ======================================================================
# NMI: saving the fault memory on power loss (F5A3-F5DB)
# ======================================================================
head F5A3
|NMI — triggered when the supply voltage drops (ignition switched off) [assumed].
|The code bytes $8000-$8002 and the counters $802B, $802C are copied into the CPU's
|internal RAM $41-$45, and their sum goes into $40. This RAM is powered from
|permanent positive (pin 33) and keeps the faults with the ignition off.
|At the next switch-on the copy is checked against the sum and restored (D13C).
