# ======================================================================
head D322
|ENGINE SPEED. Each tick the chip counts the ring gear teeth (G28), registers $0C/$0D -> $8026/$8027.
|$8018 — engine speed in units (≈22…24 rpm per unit [assumed]). From 31 units upwards —
|the count of the last tick as is; below 31 — the average over 8 ticks (during cranking
|the count is small and jumps). More than 255 — 255.
|$8098 accumulates teeth between G4 marks: 540 without a mark — suspicion
|and G4 fault (2112). The mark is handled by the interrupt (CC83).
