# ======================================================================
# Task 0: cold start valve N17 (D3A6-D737). PORT6.5 = 0 — open.
# ======================================================================
head D3A6
|N17 — COLD START VALVE. All times in ticks (≈10 ms).
|Altitude: $802D = point index for atmospheric pressure $8004 on axis C2B0
|(128 122 109 102): 0 — at sea level (> 122), 3 — high altitude (≤ 102).
|Modes (they work only after the first synchronisation, $8075.0):
|1) Test 4443: open for 2 ticks, closed for 98, 1000 ticks in total (10 s).
|2) Cold engine start (colder than ≈ +37 °C, $8075.4 = 0), until the
|   post-start delay has expired: duration from the lowest temperature $807B —
|   C664 (120 50 10 0) × 10 ticks over axis C660 (216 205 169 90), reduced
|   in proportion to ($8079 - $801D) / $8079, where $8079 comes from C66C (214 154 79 29).
|   Pulses by altitude: open C2B4 / closed C2B8 = 255/0 (at sea level —
|   continuously), 20/5, 10/10, 5/10.
|3) After start (colder than ≈ +4 °C, $8075.3 = 0): C674 (30 20 10 0) × 10 ticks
|   over axis C670 (211 205 189 169), pulses 5 open / 10 closed.
|4) Hot start (hotter than ≈ 100 °C, $8075.2 = 1): wait 200 ticks, then
|   10 open / 30 closed until 400 ticks have expired (C6C3, C6C5, C6C6, C6C8).
|5) Pressure rise (after modes 2-4, engine colder than ≈ 65 °C, throttle not
|   closed): pressure increase over 40 ms ($8073) -> opening time from C678/C680,
|   weighted by temperature (C690 -> C694). The second output ($8077.6) is the flag
|   "enrichment took place" for the mixture.
|Flags: $8075.7 — start mode in progress, .6 — start mode finished,
|.5 — after-start mode finished; $8076.7 — valve open (mode 4),
|.5 and .3 — modes 2-4 completed. $80AA — how many ticks are left, $80AC — pulse
|phase timer.
|Note: bits 0 and 1 of $8076 (D3F5-D430) compare the altitude index 0…3 with
|thresholds 28 and 26, so they are always cleared; the branches depending on them never run.
|Proof (checked by a script over the whole code, 2026-11-18):
| - D3F5 is entered only from D3B6 (B = altitude index from AXIS_DN, 0…3) and
|   by fall-through from D3ED (B = 0); D3F5-D430 is passed before every D475;
| - $8076 is written only by D3FE-D42E, D447, D627, D648; D627/D648 write A,
|   obtained from $8076 at D475, and bits 0/1 are not set on the way;
| - there is no indexed write with offset $76 and no 16-bit write to $8075 anywhere.
|Bit 2 is set only at D63B, which is reached only with bit 1 — so also never (see the header).
|Branch D5A8-D5B5 does not run because of calibration C78F = 0 (in another firmware it may).
|The only caveat: if a tester can write to RAM over the K-line, it could
|set these bits manually (the KW1281 commands have not been analysed yet).
D3A6 atmospheric pressure axis C2B0
D3A9 4 points
D3AB point index (A = $8004)
D3AE $802D = altitude 0…3
D3B1 flags $8003
