# ======================================================================
# Task 0: KW1281 diagnostics — 5-baud address reception, block exchange (D889-DAFE)
# ======================================================================
head D889
|5-BAUD ADDRESS RECEPTION — over the L-line (pin 5, PORT5.6), not over K!
|Only at engine speed ≤ 80 units (C7A7). A falling edge on the line is the start bit:
|wait 30 ticks (middle of the first data bit), then 8 bits every
|20 ticks (bit = 200 ms), least significant first, then the stop bit (line = 1).
|Address $01 (engine) received — open a session ($80F6.3).
|This gives the tick length: at 5 baud a bit = 200 ms = 20 ticks, so a tick ≈ 10 ms;
|reading in the middle of the bit tolerates an error of up to ≈ ±10 %.
|Cells: $80F6 — session state (bit 3 open, 2 — level of the L-line
|on the previous tick, bits 7-4 — phase of sending the sync bytes); $80F8 — how many
|bits are left; $80F9 — ticks until the next bit; $80FA — address being assembled.
