head D8E9
|KW1281 SESSION. After the address the unit sends the sync byte $55 (after 29 ticks),
|then the key words $01 (after 6) and $8A (after 2). The baud rate is set by
|RMCR = $06 at reset [?]. The partner acknowledges each byte with its
|inverted byte, except the last one ($03) in the block.
|$80F7: bit 7 — key words acknowledged; 6 — time to send a byte;
|5 — receiving a tester block; 1 — waiting for acknowledgement of our own byte.
|$80FB — pause before sending (ticks), $80FC — last byte,
|$80FD — response timeout (ticks, $FF — none), $80FE — byte number in the block.
|Tester block: $8104 length, $8100 counter, $8185… title and data.
|Own block: $8103 length, $8100+1 counter, $8105… title and data.
