head D0E3
|TICK (≈10 ms), from IRQ1 with interrupts enabled.
|Engine stop: after synchronisation $8025 grows every tick, a cylinder event
|resets it. 100 ticks (C78D, ≈1 s) without events means the engine has stopped:
|$8003.7; with PORT5.5 = 1 [?] the fault memory is copied to internal RAM with a checksum,
|and the program restarts (CA8E) without a full RAM check.
|Before synchronisation: with PORT5.5 = 1 and $8003.3 (copy awaits restore), if
|internal RAM power was not lost (RP5CR.7) and the checksum is correct, codes and counters
|are restored from the copy; otherwise a full restart (CA88).
