head E8F5
|BOOST REDUCTION by temperatures, subtracted from the duty cycle:
|by G42 (axis C758 = 185 175 165 137 -> C75C = 83 38 13 13; colder means more;
|(snapshot $806C - 146) is added to G42 if the snapshot is cold)
|plus by G62 (axis C760 = 216 … 21 -> C768 = 89 89 89 81 71 64 25 0; cold
|engine means more), and with $8066.5 (engine hot) by hot engine time
|(~$80B1, axis C770 -> C778 = 64 … 0). Per SSP: below +10 °C boost is reduced,
|an open circuit in G42 (−20 °C) keeps boost low.
|The integrator does not drop below the reduction. A remainder below 224/65536 becomes zero.
|Limits C7A9 = 0 … C7AA = 255.
