# ======================================================================
# RESET (RES, SWI, TRAP, NMI failure): setup, RAM check, background loop
# (CA88-CB90)
# ======================================================================
label CA88 RESET
head CA88
|RESET. Stack $8290. A full reset checks RAM from $8000; a restart after
|engine stop (D12A) checks from $8005 to keep the codes ($8000-$8002) and
|atmospheric pressure ($8004).
|CPU registers: RMCR = $06 (SCI speed [?]), RP5CR = $C1 (internal RAM,
|IRQ1), TRCSR1 = $1A (receive, transmit, receive interrupt), TCSR1 = $18 (capture
|and compare 1 interrupts [assumed]), TCSR2 = $09 (output OC1 = N7 [assumed]), PORT2 = $20,
|PORT6 = $20 (N17 closed, pump off), P2DDR = $02 (P21-P27 outputs),
|P6DDR = $F9 (P62, P61 are inputs: coding, Hall).
CA88 stack
CA8B RAM check from $8000
CA8E RMCR
CA90 SCI speed
CA92 RP5CR = $C1
CA94 old value (bit 7 = RAM power was kept)
CA96 store
CA98 SCI: receive, transmit, receive interrupt
CA9A store
CA9C timer 1
CA9E store
CAA0 timer 1, part 2
CAA2 store
CAA4 PORT2.5 = 1
CAA6 store
CAA8 PORT6.5 = 1 (N17 closed), PORT6.6 = 0 (pump off)
CAAA store
CAAC P21-P27 are outputs
CAAE store
CAB0 P60, P63-P67 are outputs
CAB2 store
CAB4 start of RAM check
CAB5 old RP5CR
