CB79 store
CB7B enable interrupts
label CB7C BG_LOOP
head CB7C
|BACKGROUND LOOP: all the time not taken by interrupts is spent on the ROM checksum.
|The sum of all bytes $C000-$FFFF (8 bit) must be 0, otherwise ECU fault 1111
|($8095.6). Any firmware modification must preserve this sum.
CB7C start of ROM
CB7F checksum = 0
CB80 + byte
CB82 next
CB83 up to $FFFF
CB85 checksum 0?
CB86 yes - start over
CB88 X = $8000
CB8B ROM fault (1111)
CB8E start over
table CB90 1 byte $0A without references, probably balances the ROM checksum to 0 [assumed]
table CB91 32 chip setup $0100 (number, value): 00 FF, 01 6C (108 half-teeth = 144°), 02 2D, 03 1B, 05 00, 06 05, 07 06, 08 03, 09 FF, 0A FF, 0B 00, 0C 33, 0D 76, 18 04, 19 00, 1F 00
E39E sensor open circuit - without lambda
DD03 end of task 0 - to the dispatcher

# ======================================================================
# Timer, SCI and IRQ2 interrupts (F5DC-F725), test exit (F726)
# ======================================================================
label F5DC OCF
head F5DC
|OCF - timer 1 compare.
|OC1: PWM for N7 on pin P21 (contact 8). Period 21400 E clocks (1.536 MHz) =
|71.8 Hz. On for $805D clocks, off for 21400 - $805D; the output level
|toggles by itself (OLVL1).
|OC2: every 7812 clocks (5.09 ms) one step of the slow PWM for N80: 32 steps = 163 ms,
|for the first $8064 steps chip register $0B = FF (N80 open), for the rest 00.
F5DC timer status, part 2
F5DE compare 2?
F5E0 yes - N80
F5E2 read (clears the OC1 flag)
F5E4 "on" time
F5E7 level 1 now?
F5EA yes - next edge after "on"
F5EC period 21400
F5EF - "on" = "off"
F5F2 toggle the level at the next match
F5F5 + to the match moment
F5F7 new moment
F5F9 exit
F5FA timer counter
F5FC + 7812 (5.09 ms)
F5FF next compare 2
F601 N80 PWM step
F604 32?
F606 yes - from the start
F608 below the duty cycle?
F60B yes - open
F60D closed: 00
F60F continue
F611 step 0
F612 duty cycle
F615 zero - closed
F617 open: FF
F619 step + 1
F61A store
F61D synchronised?
F61F check
F622 no - leave alone
F624 chip register $0B (N80)
F626 store
F629 exit
label F62A CMI
head F62A
|CMI - timer 2 match: software PWM for N75 on PORT2.6 (contact 19).
|The "on" phase lasts $8067 timer 2 counts, the "off" phase 255 - $8067.
|0 means always off, 255 always on. The frequency depends on the timer 2 prescaler
|(TCSR3, E760) [?].
F62A clear the match flag
F62D port 2
F62F N75 on now?
F631 yes
F633 duty cycle
F636 0 - leave off
F638 255?
F63A yes - switch on permanently
F63C switch on
F63E store
F640 "on" time
F643 to the timer
F645 duty cycle
F648 255?
F64A yes - leave on
F64C switch off
F64E store
F650 255
F652 - duty cycle = "off"
F655 to the timer
F657 switch off
F659 store
F65B switch on
F65D store
F65F phase duration to timer 2
label F661 TOF
head F661
|TOF and the empty end of CMI do nothing.
F661 exit
label F662 IRQ2
head F662
|IRQ2 - one-shot measurement [?]: disable IRQ2, $80F4 = |chip reg. $00 - 94|.
|IRQ2 is enabled at CDF9 (Hall high and $806E.4). $80F4 is used by the lamp
|in tester mode (F49D).
